Subject: main.c: use the POSIX process-group path on substrate

main.c's per-OS cascade has no substrate entry, so USE_SYSV_PGRP is
unset and xterm takes the BSD branch that calls the 2-argument
setpgrp(0,0).  Substrate's setpgrp(2) is the POSIX no-argument form;
select USE_SYSV_PGRP (and USE_SYSV_SIGNALS) as for Linux.

--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -158,6 +158,11 @@
 #ifdef HAVE_PTY_H
 #include <pty.h>
 #endif
+#endif
+
+#ifdef __substrate__
+#define USE_SYSV_PGRP		/* substrate has POSIX setsid/setpgid */
+#define USE_SYSV_SIGNALS
 #endif
 
 #ifdef __CYGWIN__
